  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oshkosh Defense obligated $815M in FY2026 to date, across 4,669 awards with an average award size of $175K. Oshkosh Defense obligations are down 44.9% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years. Oshkosh Defense recorded larger past yearly totals: $2.2B in FY21, $1.6B in FY22, $2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $1.5B in FY25. Oshkosh Defense sales in FY2026 to date are concentrated in Truck Trailer Manufacturing at $564M and Heavy Duty Truck Manufacturing at $115M. Oshkosh Defense also recorded activity in Hardware Manufacturing at $28.1M, Motor Vehicle Body Manufacturing at $22.7M, and Other Engine Equipment Manufacturing at $17.8M. Oshkosh Defense has a single dominant recorded buyer in FY2026 to date, the Department of Defense at $815M, with the General Services Administration showing $243. This snapshot covers fiscal-year-to-date obligations and shows where federal buying has focused so far in the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is Oshkosh Defense federal revenue right now?",
        "body": "Oshkosh Defense obligations are concentrated in a few places. The Department of Defense accounts for $815M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Truck Trailer Manufacturing accounts for $564M and Heavy Duty Truck Manufacturing accounts for $115M. Total obligations for the fiscal year to date are $815M across 4,669 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Oshkosh Defense performance trended year over year?",
        "body": "Oshkosh Defense obligations are down 44.9% year over year. Oshkosh Defense obligations peaked in recent years at $2.2B in FY21 and $2B in FY23, then moved to $1.3B in FY24 and $1.5B in FY25 before reaching $815M in FY26 to date. The current-year total is a fiscal-year-to-date figure rather than a full-year total."
      }
    ]
